#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "collector's edition book"
msgid_plural "collector's edition books"
msgstr[0] ""

#. ~ Description for collector's edition book
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A unique, valuable book that has been kept as a collector's item."
msgstr "一本獨特的，有價值的書，作為收藏家的收藏。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of Charles Dickens' \"A Tale of "
"Two Cities\"."
msgstr "這是查爾斯狄更斯的“雙城記”的高品質皮革裝訂副本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very old but well-preserved copy of Charles Dickens' \"Oliver "
"Twist\"."
msgstr "這是查爾斯狄更斯的“孤雛淚”的一個非常古老但保存完好的副本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This high-quality copy of Jane Austen's \"Pride and Prejudice\" is dog-eared"
" and looks to have been read many times."
msgstr "這本簡奧斯丁的“傲慢與偏見”的高品質副本是有多處書頁折角，看起來已被多次閱讀。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty, hardcover print of William Shinderling's \"Vanity before "
"Justice\" with beautiful illustrations."
msgstr ""
"這是威廉·辛德林（William Shinderling）的“正義之前的虛榮”（Vanity before "
"Justice）的精美印刷版，附有精美的插圖。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Jane Austen's \"Sense and Sensibility\" has a certificate of "
"authenticity declaring it to be an early edition.  It would have been worth "
"an enormous amount of money, not long ago."
msgstr "簡奧斯汀的“理智與情感”副本，隨附真品證書，宣稱它是早期版本。它本來值一大筆錢，但是現在...。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an excellent quality copy of \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" by Harper "
"Lee."
msgstr "這是哈波·李的“梅岡城故事”的高品質副本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of F. Scott Fitzgerald's \"The "
"Great Gatsby.\""
msgstr "這是F·史考特·費茲傑羅的“大亨小傳”的高品質皮革裝訂副本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty, hardcover print of Michael Abanaderly's opus, \"Lady "
"Wanderlust\".  It is over a hundred years old, but doesn't look it."
msgstr "這沉重的精裝書是Michael Abanaderly的作品“Lady Wanderlust”。它有一百多年的歷史，但看起來像全新的。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Ray Bradbury's \"Fahrenheit 451\" has a certificate of "
"authenticity declaring it to be an early edition.  It would have been worth "
"an enormous amount of money, not long ago."
msgstr "雷·道格拉斯·布萊伯利的“華氏451度”副本，隨附真品證書，宣稱它是早期版本。它本來值一大筆錢，但是現在...。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This high-quality copy of \"Pride and Prejudice and Zombies\" has been "
"autographed by the author."
msgstr "這本高品質的“傲慢與偏見與殭屍”副本已由作者親筆簽名。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of \"The Adventures of Huckleberry"
" Finn\" by Mark Twain.  It contains some margin notes which themselves are "
"quite old, and look to have been done by a scholar of some sort."
msgstr "這是馬克吐溫的“頑童歷險記”的高品質皮革裝訂副本。它包含一些本身相當陳舊的頁緣註釋，並且看起來是由某位學者完成的"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very nice print of Bram Stoker's \"Dracula\".  It has a "
"certificate of authenticity with it that declares it a genuine early "
"edition."
msgstr "這是伯蘭·史杜克的“德古拉”完美的印刷版。它有一個真品證書，宣稱它是一個真正的早期版本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Douglas Adams' \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" has a "
"certificate of authenticity declaring it to be a first edition, and is "
"autographed by the author himself."
msgstr "這本道格拉斯亞當斯的“銀河便車指南“有一份真品證書，宣稱它是第一版，並由作者親自簽名。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of the well-known classic \"Dark "
"Days Ahead\", by K. G. Ranade."
msgstr "這是由K. G. Ranade著名的經典“Dark Days Ahead”的高品質皮革裝訂副本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a well-kept leather bound copy of \"Oryx and Crake\" by Margaret "
"Atwood.  Inscribed in the inner cover is a faded note wishing the owner a "
"happy birthday."
msgstr ""
"這是瑪格麗特阿特伍德（Margaret Atwood）保存完好的“Oryx and "
"Crake”皮革裝訂副本。內封面上刻有一張褪色的紙條，祝主人生日快樂。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This bright orange hardcover copy of \"1984\" by George Orwell has been "
"carefully preserved, and appears to be a first or second edition judging "
"from the publisher's information."
msgstr "喬治·奧威爾（George Orwell）的這本亮橙色封面精裝版“1984”經過精心保存，從出版商的信息來看似乎是第一版或第二版。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very nice copy of \"Lady Chatterly's Lover\", probably quite "
"expensive in the days before the apocalypse."
msgstr "這是“查特利夫人的情人”的一個狀況良好的副本，在災變之前可能相當昂貴。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high quality early edition hardcover copy of \"The Handmaid's "
"Tale\" by Margaret Atwood, signed by the author."
msgstr "這是由作者簽名的瑪格麗特阿特伍德的“使女的故事”的高品質早期版精裝本。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This ancient and worn book looks to be an 18th or early 19th century "
"handwritten copy of \"Don Quixote\".  In the days of book traders it would "
"have been worth an absolute fortune.  Now it's either a priceless piece of "
"history, some light reading before bed, or excellent kindling."
msgstr ""
"這本古老而破舊的書看起來是18世紀或19世紀初“唐吉訶德”的手抄本。在圖書交易有市場的災變前，它本來值得一切。現在它要麼是無價的歷史文物，或是輕鬆的床邊讀物。同時也是出色的燃料。"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a first edition copy of Terry Pratchett's \"The Colour of Magic\".  "
"In the inner cover is a handwritten note that reads \"To Chris, thanks for "
"believing I could do it.  Best regards, Terry.\""
msgstr "這是泰瑞·普萊契的“The Colour of Magic”的初版。在內封面是一個手寫的筆記，寫著“給克里斯，感謝你對我的信心。泰瑞上。”"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Economicon of Dobbs"
msgid_plural "copies of The Economicon"
msgstr[0] ""

#. ~ Description for The Economicon of Dobbs
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"These are the prescriptures Pile 18 Disk sg30 File 14.  \"Look, small brain "
"of pink earth inside my null-grasping, and she/he receives Logos; and it lay"
" with the Wor.\""
msgstr ""

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Bobliographon"
msgid_plural "copies of The Bobliographon"
msgstr[0] ""

#. ~ Description for The Bobliographon
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The back cover of this cheaply published paperback reads: \"These newly-"
"released SubGenius revelations will SHOCK those who think they know Bob!  "
"Unpredictables are not alone and possess amazing hidden powers of their own!"
